---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
	title="Changelog — Signalint"
	description="Published Signalint package versions and the current GitHub Releases record."
>
	<section class="section">
		<div class="shell prose">
			<header class="page-heading">
				<p class="eyebrow">Release history</p>
				<h1>Changelog</h1>
				<p class="lede">Package publication history, newest first. Formal release notes will be linked from GitHub Releases as they are created.</p>
			</header>

			<div class="note">
				<p>
					The <a href="https://github.com/TranQui004/signalint/releases">GitHub Releases feed</a>
					currently contains no release objects. The entries below use the public npm registry's
					publication timestamps and link to the corresponding package versions.
				</p>
			</div>

			<div class="timeline">
				<article class="release">
					<div class="release-meta">
						<a href="https://www.npmjs.com/package/signalint-mcp/v/0.2.0">v0.2.0</a>
						<time datetime="2026-08-01">1 Aug 2026</time>
					</div>
					<div>
						<h2>Setup command and current documentation</h2>
						<ul>
							<li>Added <code>npx signalint-mcp init</code> for project and MCP-client detection.</li>
							<li>Published the current architecture, contributor, security, and historical design documentation.</li>
							<li>Includes all pre-launch cache, fan-out, storage-bound, and security hardening merged before publication.</li>
						</ul>
					</div>
				</article>
				<article class="release">
					<div class="release-meta">
						<a href="https://www.npmjs.com/package/signalint-mcp/v/0.1.0">v0.1.0</a>
						<time datetime="2026-08-01">1 Aug 2026</time>
					</div>
					<div>
						<h2>Initial npm publication</h2>
						<ul>
							<li>Local stdio MCP server with Oxlint, TypeScript, and optional Biome adapters.</li>
							<li>SQLite caching, rule-based clustering, and session loop detection.</li>
							<li>Claude Code, Cursor, Antigravity, and direct CLI setup paths.</li>
						</ul>
					</div>
				</article>
			</div>
		</div>
	</section>
</BaseLayout>
